433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 255 0 R
/T (Certain gut bacteria make an enzyme that snips that tag back off. The estrogen becomes active again and is reabsorbed instead of leaving. Researchers have taken thirty-five of these bacterial enzymes, tested them directly, solved their structures, and blocked the reaction with an inhibitor. The mechanism is not a theory. This enzyme is called Beta-glucaronidase and if you have note taken a stool test to know if this is happening that is a great place to start.)
/E (Certain gut bacteria make an enzyme that snips that tag back off. The estrogen becomes active again and is reabsorbed instead of leaving. Researchers have taken thirty-five of these bacterial enzymes, tested them directly, solved their structures, and blocked the reaction with an inhibitor. The mechanism is not a theory. This enzyme is called Beta-glucaronidase and if you have note taken a stool test to know if this is happening that is a great place to start.)
